- Client request timeout: 25 seconds at Nginx.
- Gateway server timeout: 30 seconds.
- Downstream GraphQL requests inherit request headers and use a 20-second fetch timeout.
- No retries occur for GraphQL mutations.
- Query retries are deliberately omitted in this baseline because retries can duplicate side effects when downstream operation classification is incorrect.
- Ordering is preserved within one GraphQL request; no cross-request ordering guarantee exists.
- Gateway configuration changes are durable before reload, but a restart is required before they become active.